shape theory.physics.mirror.projections : theory.physics.mirror, theory.physics.u1, theory.physics.su2, theory.physics.su3, theory.landscape {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// The Nine Projection Families (02d §10).
// 3 bases x 3 chirality options = 9 projections.
// All FORCED by the Laws of Coherence, not merely possible.
//
// Three possible bases (which gauge structure is foundational):
//   Psi family: U(1) base. U(1) -> SU(2) -> SU(3). This is us.
//   Phi family: SU(2) base. SU(2) -> SU(3), no independent U(1).
//   Xi family:  SU(3) base. SU(3) only (SU(2), U(1) embedded).
//
// Three chirality options (all required):
//   A: forces rotation one direction -> matter.
//   B: forces rotation opposite direction -> antimatter.
//   Null: anti-rotation field (prevents rotation) -> dark energy.
//
// The nine projections:
//   Psi (us):     U(1) + chirality A.  Visible matter.
//   Psi-mirror:   U(1) + chirality B.  Dark matter (antimatter twin).
//   Psi-null:     U(1) + null.         Dark energy.
//   Phi:          SU(2) + chirality A.  Dark matter.
//   Phi-mirror:   SU(2) + chirality B.  Dark matter.
//   Phi-null:     SU(2) + null.         Dark energy.
//   Xi:           SU(3) + chirality A.  Dark matter.
//   Xi-mirror:    SU(3) + chirality B.  Dark matter.
//   Xi-null:      SU(3) + null.         Dark energy.
//
// Breakdown: 1 visible, 5 dark matter, 3 dark energy.
//
// All 9 share the same 3D Planck lattice (gravity is the spatial
// projection). They differ in internal structure only.
// Dark matter and dark energy interact gravitationally but not
// through our gauge forces: same lattice, different internal
// projections.
//
// QM is projection-specific: only Psi and Psi-mirror (U(1) base)
// have wave propagation as their coherence-checking mechanism.
// Only they have superposition, interference, quantum mechanics.
// Phi and Xi families may be fundamentally deterministic.
//
// The cosmic 68/27/5 energy distribution:
//   ~68% dark energy (3 null-chirality projections)
//   ~27% dark matter (5 chirality A/B non-U(1) projections)
//   ~5% visible matter (1 projection: us)
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.mirror, theory.physics.u1,
//               theory.physics.su2, theory.physics.su3,
//               theory.landscape (every coherent structure persists)
  """
}
